<< /A << /BBox [ 63.4394 440.391 531.383 761.443 ] /O /Layout >> /Alt (Infographic comparing specified reference dosimetry and candidate AI-assisted modules for absorbed-dose estimation in medical imaging. The left panel details five steps: quantitative imaging, human-reviewed segmentation, time-activity modeling, absorbed-dose calculation, and reference absorbed-dose reporting. The right panel outlines AI-assisted modules, including reduced time-point inference, automated segmentation, kinetic/TIA prediction, dose-map prediction, and uncertainty-aware reporting. Central section highlights validation conditions and shared clinical goals, emphasizing accuracy, external validation, uncertainty assessment, and final human approval. Schematic illustrations support each workflow step, demonstrating imaging, activity curves, segmentation, dose calculations, and AI outputs.) /K 38 /Lang (en-EN) /P 23 0 R /Pg 266 0 R /S /Figure /Type /StructElem >>
